direction: down

title: |md
  ## Ringbuf: producers, consumers, drops
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

producers: "Producers (BPF on N CPUs)\n\nEach bpf_ringbuf_reserve():\n- cmpxchg producer_pos forward\n- if (producer_pos - consumer_pos\n    > size) return NULL  ← drop!\n- else: return slot pointer\n\nYou must check for NULL.\nNULL = ringbuf full =\nuserspace is too slow." {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
}

ring: "Ring memory\n\nTwo pointers:\n- producer_pos (atomic, by reserve)\n- consumer_pos (by userspace)\n\nRecords each have:\n- 8-byte header (size + busy bit)\n- payload (your bytes)\n\nDrops happen when prod - cons > size.\nNo queueing, no back-pressure." {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

consumer: "Consumer (userspace)\n\nring_buffer__poll(rb, timeout_ms):\n- read producer_pos\n- while (cons_pos < prod_pos):\n    - skip busy records (in-flight)\n    - call your handler() per record\n    - advance consumer_pos\n- returns # records consumed\n\nSlow consumer = drops. Either:\n- increase ring size\n- reduce per-record work in handler\n- filter more aggressively in BPF" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
}

producers -> ring: "reserve / submit" {style.stroke: "#16a34a"}
ring -> consumer: "poll" {style.stroke: "#16a34a"}
consumer -> ring: "advance" {style.stroke: "#16a34a"; style.stroke-dash: 4}

drop: "BPF_RB_FORCE_WAKEUP\nflag on submit:\nwakes consumer immediately\n(useful for low-latency events)" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

consumer -> drop {style.stroke-dash: 4}
